{"title":"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Non-rigorous_speed_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Non-rigorous speed solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a square and circumscribed about another square as shown. Which fraction is closest to the ratio of the circle's shaded area to the area between the two squares?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1e342aed303af8799c42492f077aab15037276.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw((-1,-1)--(-1,1)--(1,1)--(1,-1)--cycle,gray,black); filldraw(Circle((0,0),1), mediumgray,black); filldraw((-1,0)--(0,1)--(1,0)--(0,-1)--cycle,white,black);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c7aba5214bbfffde1cc6b0489285f9f1485bef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}2\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"359\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the smaller square is one half of the product of its diagonals. Note that the distance from a corner of the smaller square to the center is equivalent to the circle's radius so the diagonal is equal to the diameter: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16fc1cf5fd867cb9f877550617991777c2b26f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot  2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The circle's shaded area is the area of the smaller square subtracted from the area of the circle: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14bfc9cd0753cf0423ea1e4de8fb0d31124a37a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi - 2.$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>If you draw the diagonals of the smaller square, you will see that the larger square is split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> congruent half-shaded squares. The area between the squares is equal to the area of the smaller square: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Approximating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f85268a04ce83fadccec65583d28ed605392e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.14,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> the ratio of the circle's shaded area to the area between the two squares is about\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6f156f898452f44a65f7d51850093427f09644.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi-2}{2} \\approx \\frac{3.14-2}{2} = \\frac{1.14}{2} \\approx \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac12}\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the ratio of the circle's shaded area to the area between the squares to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> they would have to be approximately the same size. For any ratio larger than that, the circle's shaded area must be greater. However, we can clearly see that the circle's shaded area is part of the area between the squares, and is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c4ca99359d88f25a1fe42ca6bd5d8ce7211bea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />. The ratio must be less than 1, because the area inside the circle is less than the total shaded area, and the only answer choice that fits that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7e0167ba754e824f63be04bbcba6f1a8d0cf7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\nNote that this solution is not rigorous, because we still should show that the ratio is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Slightly edited by rwpiano\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set the side length of the bigger square to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \nThen the area of the big square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f6f68c151b8eda90a1d5e79636dc9b994f980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^2 =64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> and \nthe area of the small square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6aba683c755d72dfc6fd7f27d69916c85dd9e53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4\\sqrt{2})^2  = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />, \nmaking the difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \nThe area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a66c53514f5e6b6b6d096fe617320424b897b479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/3129b1de4fff4c0120a0c752c648d18a64068979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> or about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \nKnowing the area of the small square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c476befc9990f9c464b8e755746bcdde41fdcef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48-32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \nThe area of the big square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />. \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78cc668007077c97d27a2e8876caf25509ca21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32/64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c4ca99359d88f25a1fe42ca6bd5d8ce7211bea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Non-rigorous_speed_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Non-rigorous_speed_solution)\">Solution 4 (Non-rigorous speed solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Non-rigorous speed solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that that the shaded area of the circle is existent only between the gap between the two squares. This implies that the shaded area is less than the gap, and the only answer that shows that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d1171c31c075fa575ff889fe071f3123c198fb71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n- by nickelslordm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PR-45YsyBGM\">https://youtu.be/PR-45YsyBGM</a>  Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=1759\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=1759</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Nsm9bggy30g\">https://youtu.be/Nsm9bggy30g</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8\">2011 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017000704\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 228/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2239/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 136/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5596/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.405      1 -total\n 58.79%    7.293      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 39.50%    4.900      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10464:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017000704 and revision id 271595. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}